## ISS-008: update-server serves downloads without security headers

### File
`/root/Redball/update-server/server.js`

### Original (top imports)
```javascript
const morgan = require('morgan');
```

### Replacement
```javascript
const morgan = require('morgan');
const helmet = require('helmet');
```

### Original (middleware setup)
```javascript
const app = express();
app.set('trust proxy', 1); // Enable trust proxy for rate limiting (needed behind Cloudflare/reverse proxy)
const server = http.createServer(app);
```

### Replacement
```javascript
const app = express();
app.use(helmet());
app.set('trust proxy', 1); // Enable trust proxy for rate limiting (needed behind Cloudflare/reverse proxy)
const server = http.createServer(app);
```

### Also update
`/root/Redball/update-server/package.json` dependencies to add `"helmet": "^7.0.0"`, then run `npm install`.

### Reason
Adds standard security headers (CSP, X-Frame-Options, X-Content-Type-Options, etc.) to the update server and public downloads.

### Verification
`npm install` + `npm test` + inspect response headers with `curl -I`.
